        <p>These Terms of Service (“Terms”) form an agreement between EduCore Education Technology (“EduCore”, “we”, “our”, or “us”) and the school, organisation, or individual that accesses the EduCore public website, web portals, Android application, APIs, downloads, and related support services (together, the “Service”).</p>
        <p>Our <a href="{{ route('legal.privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a> explains how personal data is handled and is incorporated into these Terms. Additional written order forms, invoices, school policies, or feature-specific notices may also apply. If a signed agreement conflicts with these public Terms, the signed agreement controls to the extent of that conflict.</p>

        <h2 id="agreement">1. Agreement, Eligibility, and Authority</h2>
        <p>By registering, accepting an invitation, downloading the Android application, or using the Service, you confirm that you have read and accepted these Terms.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A person registering a school must be at least 18 years old, have legal capacity, and be authorised to bind that school or organisation.</li>
            <li>A student or other minor may use only an account created or authorised by the relevant school and subject to appropriate parent, guardian, and school oversight.</li>
            <li>If you do not accept these Terms, you must not register for or use the Service.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="accounts">2. Accounts, Unified Login, and Role-Based Access</h2>
        <p>EduCore uses a unified authentication service and role-based access control (“RBAC”). A user’s visible modules and permitted actions depend on the user’s verified school, role, permissions, assignments, and linked records.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You must provide accurate registration details and keep them current.</li>
            <li>You must protect passwords, devices, reset links, API tokens, QR codes, and any other credentials issued to you.</li>
            <li>You must not share an individual account, impersonate another person, or use another role’s access.</li>
            <li>You must notify the relevant school administrator and EduCore promptly if you suspect unauthorised access.</li>
            <li>School administrators are responsible for creating, assigning, reviewing, disabling, and deleting school user access.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>EduCore may require password changes, verification, account recovery, or session revocation where reasonably necessary for security.</p>

        <h2 id="service">3. Current Service Scope</h2>
        <p>Depending on role, configuration, and availability, the Service may include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>school onboarding, records, classes, subjects, sessions, terms, admissions, transfers, promotion, alumni, and portal accounts;</li>
            <li>student and staff attendance, timetables, lesson planning, scores, gradebooks, exams, CBT, report cards, certificates, conduct, and academic reporting;</li>
            <li>fee structures, bills, invoices, parent payments, receipts, expenses, accounting reports, staff salary settings, payroll, and payslips;</li>
            <li>staff HR, leave, announcements, messages, notifications, reminders, identity cards, and document or photograph uploads;</li>
            <li>restricted health records and health visits, transport routes, vehicles, drivers, manifests, and student transport assignments;</li>
            <li>platform school and plan administration, payment review, agent registration, referrals, and commissions; and</li>
            <li>the native Android application and a bridge that can open the complete web platform.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Some features require a compatible device, internet connection, school configuration, user permission, or a supported third-party provider. Displaying a module does not override RBAC or create a right to use it.</p>

        <h2 id="school">4. School Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>Each subscribing school controls its educational and operational records and is responsible for:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>having authority and a lawful basis to collect, enter, use, and disclose staff, student, applicant, parent, health, payroll, transport, and other school data;</li>
            <li>giving required notices and obtaining required parental, guardian, employee, or other consent or authorisation;</li>
            <li>keeping records, class assignments, parent-child links, financial settings, health and transport information, and user roles accurate;</li>
            <li>configuring attendance times, geo-fencing, fee structures, assessments, payroll settings, transport and health workflows, and school communications lawfully;</li>
            <li>reviewing and approving reports, results, bills, payroll, refunds, notices, and operational decisions before relying on them;</li>
            <li>training authorised users and removing access promptly when a user changes role or leaves; and</li>
            <li>maintaining any records, licences, policies, insurance, professional personnel, and regulatory approvals required for school operations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A school is responsible for activity performed through its authorised accounts, except to the extent directly caused by EduCore’s breach of these Terms or applicable law.</p>

        <h2 id="acceptable">5. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You may use the Service only for lawful school, educational, administrative, family, support, or authorised platform purposes. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>access another school, child, user, module, record, or API without permission;</li>
            <li>bypass RBAC, tenant controls, rate limits, authentication, payment controls, or other safeguards;</li>
            <li>upload unlawful, harmful, fraudulent, defamatory, infringing, malicious, or misleading content;</li>
            <li>enter false attendance, academic, health, payroll, payment, transport, identity, or agent records;</li>
            <li>use scraping, bots, vulnerability scanning, automated extraction, or reverse engineering without prior written authorisation, except where a restriction is prohibited by law;</li>
            <li>introduce malware, disrupt the Service, overload infrastructure, or interfere with another user;</li>
            <li>sell, sublicense, lease, copy, or commercially exploit the Service except under an authorised EduCore agent or partner arrangement; or</li>
            <li>use children’s records, sensitive personal data, or contact information for advertising, harassment, discrimination, or unrelated profiling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="pricing">6. Pricing, Capacity, School Fees, and Payments</h2>
        <div class="pricing-card">
            <div class="price-option"><span>Up to 50 active students</span><strong>Free</strong><small>All published EduCore features included</small></div>
            <div class="price-option"><span>Above 50 active students</span><strong>&#8358;300</strong><small>for every active student, per academic term</small></div>
        </div>
        <h3>6.1 Platform subscription calculation</h3>
        <p>A school with 50 or fewer active students is eligible for the free plan. Once a school has more than 50 active students, the termly subscription is calculated at &#8358;300 multiplied by the school’s total active-student count for that term. The first 50 students are not deducted from the paid calculation. There are no percentage discounts, and all published features are included, subject to these Terms, RBAC, technical availability, and lawful configuration.</p>
        <p>Active-student count is determined from the Service when capacity, billing, or renewal is calculated. A school must not misclassify active students to avoid payment. Annual amounts, where offered, equal three termly amounts unless a written invoice states otherwise.</p>
        <h3>6.2 Invoices, taxes, and subscription payment</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Paid capacity or continued paid access may require payment by the date on the applicable invoice.</li>
            <li>Amounts are stated in Nigerian naira unless otherwise specified. Any applicable tax or separately disclosed provider charge may be added as required by law or the selected channel.</li>
            <li>Subscription payments are generally final after paid capacity or a service period has been enabled, except for duplicate transactions, confirmed processing errors, an express written agreement, or a refund required by law.</li>
            <li>We may change future pricing by publishing the new price and giving reasonable notice to affected paid schools. A change does not alter an already paid term.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>6.3 Parent payments and school fee collection</h3>
        <p>Schools, not EduCore, determine student fees, bills, discounts, refunds, and payment instructions. EduCore provides technology to present bills, initiate supported payments, receive provider status, and reconcile school records. Transactions may be handled by providers such as Monnify, Paystack, Flutterwave, banks, or other enabled channels and remain subject to the provider’s terms.</p>
        <p>A parent or payer must verify the school, student, amount, and payment reference before authorising payment. Payment disputes concerning a school charge should first be raised with the school. Processing or settlement issues may also require review by the relevant payment provider.</p>

        <h2 id="mobile">7. Android Application, Location, Camera, and Attendance</h2>
        <p>The Android application is a native companion to the Service. Users may also open the web platform through the available bridge. Device permissions are requested only when needed for a selected function.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A school may enable geo-fencing for staff attendance and configure its location and permitted radius.</li>
            <li>Users must not falsify, spoof, manipulate, or circumvent location, QR, time, identity, or attendance evidence.</li>
            <li>The camera may be used for QR scanning, profile or document upload, or an authorised live photograph for proxy attendance verification.</li>
            <li>A school must communicate its attendance and monitoring policy to staff and configure these controls lawfully.</li>
            <li>Users may deny optional permissions, but a feature that requires the denied permission may not function.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="data">8. Data, Privacy, Exports, and Security</h2>
        <p>As between EduCore and a subscribing school, the school retains its rights in the school data it lawfully submits. The school grants EduCore a limited right to host, copy, transmit, process, back up, and display that data as necessary to operate, secure, support, and improve the Service and comply with law.</p>
        <p>Personal data is handled under the <a href="{{ route('legal.privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a>. Schools and users must use exports, downloads, reports, PDFs, photographs, and API data securely. Once data is exported or shared outside the Service, the exporting party is responsible for its protection and lawful use.</p>
        <p>We use technical and organisational safeguards, but no online service is completely risk-free. Users must maintain secure devices, current contact details, confidential credentials, and appropriate internal controls.</p>

        <h2 id="ownership">9. EduCore Ownership and Limited Licence</h2>
        <p>EduCore and its licensors own the Service, software, APIs, workflows, interfaces, documentation, brand assets, templates, and other platform materials, excluding school data and third-party materials. Subject to these Terms, we grant authorised users a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to use the Service for its intended purpose during an active account.</p>
        <p>Feedback may be used to improve the Service without payment or restriction, provided we do not identify the contributor publicly without permission.</p>

        <h2>10. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>The Service may rely on hosting, email, SMS, mapping, payment, banking, device, or other third-party services. We do not control their independent systems or terms. A third-party outage, rejection, delay, policy, or error may affect a related EduCore feature. We will use reasonable efforts to diagnose supported integrations but cannot guarantee a third party’s performance.</p>

        <h2 id="availability">11. Availability, Maintenance, and Platform Changes</h2>
        <p>We aim to provide a reliable Service but do not promise uninterrupted or error-free availability unless a separate written service-level agreement says otherwise. We may deploy security updates, maintenance, repairs, improvements, or feature changes. Where practical, we will provide notice of planned material downtime or changes.</p>
        <p>We may add, modify, replace, or retire a feature where reasonably necessary for security, law, provider compatibility, platform integrity, or product development. We will seek to avoid materially reducing an already paid core service during the paid term without reasonable notice or an appropriate remedy.</p>

        <h2 id="disclaimers">12. Academic, Financial, Health, Transport, and Operational Disclaimers</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Academic:</strong> Calculations, score forms, reports, recommendations, remarks, promotion tools, and AI-assisted content are administrative aids. Schools and qualified staff must review them before publication or decision-making.</li>
            <li><strong>Financial and payroll:</strong> Billing, reconciliation, expense, payroll, pension, tax, and payslip tools do not constitute accounting, tax, banking, or legal advice. The school must verify settings, deductions, bank details, and statutory compliance.</li>
            <li><strong>Health:</strong> Health-record features support authorised school recordkeeping and do not provide diagnosis, treatment, emergency response, or medical advice. Schools remain responsible for qualified personnel and emergency procedures.</li>
            <li><strong>Transport:</strong> Route and manifest features support administration but do not operate vehicles, employ drivers, inspect vehicles, track journeys continuously, or replace transport safety obligations.</li>
            <li><strong>Communications:</strong> Delivery of email, SMS, push, or other messages can be delayed or blocked by networks, devices, providers, contact errors, or recipient settings.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="termination">13. Suspension, Termination, and Data After Closure</h2>
        <p>A school may stop using the Service and request account closure through an authorised administrator. An individual school user should contact the school administrator to close or correct the user’s account.</p>
        <p>We may restrict or suspend access where reasonably necessary because of a material breach, unlawful use, security risk, unpaid amount, false registration, attack on the Service, legal requirement, or threat to another school or user. Where appropriate, we will give notice and an opportunity to remedy the issue.</p>
        <p>On closure, access ends and the school should request any available export promptly. Data may be retained, deleted, de-identified, or placed beyond normal use according to school instructions, our Privacy Policy, backup cycles, dispute needs, and legal obligations. Terms concerning payment, ownership, confidentiality, disclaimers, liability, disputes, and lawful data retention survive closure where their nature requires.</p>

        <h2>14. Warranties</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Service is provided “as available”. We do not warrant that every feature will meet every school’s specific policy or regulatory requirement, that third-party services will always be available, or that all user-entered data and generated outputs will be accurate. Nothing in these Terms excludes a warranty or consumer right that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

        <h2 id="liability">15. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, EduCore is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, punitive, or consequential loss; loss of profit, goodwill, opportunity, or anticipated savings; or loss caused by inaccurate school data, unauthorised role assignment, insecure exports, unsupported devices, third-party services, or decisions made without appropriate review.</p>
        <p>EduCore’s aggregate liability arising from the Service will not exceed the amount paid by the affected school to EduCore for the Service during the 12 months immediately before the event giving rise to the claim. This limitation does not apply where liability cannot lawfully be limited, including liability arising from fraud or wilful misconduct where applicable.</p>

        <h2>16. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, a school agrees to defend and indemnify EduCore against third-party claims, losses, and reasonable costs arising from the school’s unlawful data, failure to obtain required authority or consent, misuse of the Service, unauthorised roles, school fees or refunds, operational decisions, or breach of these Terms, except to the extent caused by EduCore’s own breach or unlawful conduct.</p>

